   "kind": "concept",
   "body": "FOIL works on radicals unchanged. (1 + √2)(3 + √2) = 3 + √2 + 3√2 + √2·√2 = 3 + 4√2 + 2 = **5 + 4√2**. Radical terms combine like like-terms; √2 · √2 collapses to plain 2.",
   "figure": "re-foil-radicals"
  },
  {
   "id": "i1",
   "kind": "interactive",
   "body": "Track the rational part.",
   "widget": {
    "type": "numeric",
    "prompt": "For (1 + √2)(3 + √2), the rational part collects 1·3 and √2·√2. What is it?",
    "answer": 5,
    "tolerance": 0,
    "commonErrors": [
     {
      "value": 3,
      "feedback": "The Last product √2 · √2 = 2 is rational too: 3 + 2 = 5."
